gametitle=Grand Theft Auto: San Andreas (NTSC-U SLUS-20946 / CRC 399A49CA)
comment=Definitive Edition-style controls for Grand Theft Auto: San Andreas.
comment=Built for the original PS2 default control scheme. Changing the in-game control type can produce different results.
comment=Hold Select in any vehicle to temporarily restore native controls, including the D-pad for prompts that require a directional response.
comment=Aircraft: L1 and R1 stay native, R2 maps to native Cross, and physical Cross maps to native Circle/fire with full pressure.
comment=Bikes: R2 accelerates, L2 brakes, Cross/Square retain their native actions, D-pad Left/Right look left/right, and R3 looks behind.
comment=Other vehicles: R2 accelerate, L2 brake/reverse, R1 or Cross handbrake, L1 main fire, D-pad Down alternate fire, D-pad Right/Left next/previous radio, D-pad Up sub-mission/special action, Square/Circle look left/right, and R3 looks behind.
comment=On foot: R2 fires, L2 aims, L1 selects the previous weapon, and R1 selects the next weapon. D-pad and R3 stay native.
comment=Public credit: Zeroable.
comment=Control-remapping foundation based on PS2 Controller Remapper by pelvicthrustman.

[GTA-PS2-Modern-Controls\Definitive Edition Controls\1 REQUIRED - Definitive Edition vehicle controls]
description=Required vehicle controls. Bikes and aircraft use vehicle-specific layouts; all other vehicles use the standard modern layout. Hold Select in vehicles to temporarily restore native controls and D-pad input. On-foot controls remain stock unless group 2 is enabled.
author=Zeroable

